# A Page to Test the Light

This is a temporary page. It is here so the reading can be seen before the real books arrive.{pause 1.2}

Words can come {slow}slowly, one breath at a time,{/slow} or {fast}they can hurry when the moment hurries,{/fast} and then settle.{pause .8}

Some words are {hush}spoken very quietly{/hush}. Some {swell}rise as they arrive{/swell}.{breath}

A word can {tremble}shiver{/tremble}, or take on a colour: {glow eblue}the river{/glow}, {glow leaf}the leaves{/glow}, {glow gold}the cup{/glow}.

{tone stars}A note can sound at the exact place it belongs.{pause 1}

{echo}And a line can stay behind for a moment after it is said.{/echo}

---

{scene aurora}
# The second page

When a page turns, the light can change with it.{pause .6} {glow violet}This page is read under an aurora.{/glow}{pause 1.4}

{scene dawn}Real books will be placed here later, each one written in the same plain way, so any story can be read like this.
